{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_cgtk_digital_experience_platform", "label": "CGTK Digital Experience Platform Backend API", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Rafly Pratama Hudzaifah Al Syahbani", "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_zero_cost_budget_constraint", "label": "Zero Monthly Cost Budget Constraint (Rp 100,000 total)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The entire project budget is Rp 100,000 in total, not per month. This single constraint drives nearly every stack and design decision; Render (sleeps), Railway (Hobby credit is not a price, Postgres pushes it to $10-18/month, over the whole budget) and MySQL were rejected against it."}, {"id": "readme_cloudflare_workers", "label": "Cloudflare Workers Runtime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen because it has no cold start. A platform that sleeps after 15 minutes idle wakes in ~50 seconds, which is survivable on a website but fatal with a queue of students at a session gate."}, {"id": "readme_hono_router", "label": "Hono Web Framework", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Small, Web-standard, runs natively on Workers so no Node compatibility shims sit in the request path."}, {"id": "readme_supabase_postgresql", "label": "Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Free tier covers ~500 participants and 250-300 concurrent with headroom, and bundles Google sign-in plus file storage that would each otherwise be a week of work. JSONB carries the admin-defined registration form."}, {"id": "readme_postgrest_over_http", "label": "supabase-js over PostgREST HTTP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Workers have no long-lived TCP sockets. PostgREST over HTTPS means there is no connection pool to exhaust when 300 phones sync at once."}, {"id": "readme_polling_not_realtime", "label": "Polling Instead of Supabase Realtime", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The free tier caps Realtime at 200 concurrent connections against an expected peak of 250-300, and connection 201 fails silently: announcements would simply not arrive with nothing in any log to explain it. Announcements are polled every 30s and answer 204 when there is nothing new."}, {"id": "readme_zod_edge_validation", "label": "Zod Validation at the Module Edge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every request body is validated at the edge of the module so nothing unvalidated ever reaches a SQL function."}, {"id": "readme_row_level_security", "label": "Row Level Security (0011_rls.sql)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RLS denies the public anon key everything except a short list of genuinely public tables, so no browser ever needs to hold a database credential."}, {"id": "readme_worker_sole_db_client", "label": "Worker as Sole Database Client", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Worker is the only thing that talks to the database; the service role key never leaves it because that key bypasses RLS entirely."}, {"id": "readme_transactional_db_functions", "label": "Multi-Table Operations in PostgreSQL Functions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Over HTTP, 'record the scan, add the XP, write the audit row' would be three independent calls; a dropped connection between them would award XP for a check-in that does not exist, or record attendance that never earned anything. Inside a PostgreSQL function it is one transaction (db/migrations/0008_functions.sql)."}, {"id": "readme_qr_identity", "label": "QR Identity (build, verify, hash)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HMAC-signed with QR_SIGNING_SECRET; rotating that secret invalidates every issued badge. Nothing in the verification path may throw because a scanner receives whatever the camera decodes, including partial reads, and a crashed scanner stops the queue."}, {"id": "readme_local_jwt_verification", "label": "Local HS256 JWT Verification with WebCrypto", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supabase access tokens are verified locally rather than by calling Supabase, because a network round trip per scan would be the slowest part of the check-in path."}, {"id": "readme_response_envelope", "label": "Unified Response Envelope (sukses/data/error)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One envelope for every endpoint. 'pesan' is written in Indonesian for the person holding the phone and is displayed verbatim by the frontend; 'kode' is what code should branch on."}, {"id": "readme_error_code_catalog", "label": "Error Code Catalog (lib/errors.ts, ~45 codes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Messages are written for field staff, and the central error handler never leaks internals. Anything a user can trigger must have a matching code here."}, {"id": "readme_module_per_prefix_ownership", "label": "One Module Owns One Route Prefix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Administrative routes are nested under their own module (/payments/admin/... not /admin/payments/...) so one file owns one prefix and a permission mistake cannot spread outside it."}, {"id": "readme_dual_route_mounting", "label": "Dual Mounting at Root and /api/v1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every route answers both at the root and under /api/v1 because /api/v1 is the base URL the API Contract gives the frontend team. Same router, two spellings."}, {"id": "readme_kv_rate_limiting", "label": "KV Fixed-Window Rate Limiting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only active when a KV namespace is bound: 10/min auth, 30/min scanning, 5/min sync, 10/min public status lookups, 120/min otherwise."}, {"id": "readme_anti_farming_booth_key", "label": "Anti-Farming Keyed on (participant_id, booth_id)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never keyed on campus_id: in Event 3 a single table is staffed by alumni from several universities at once, so a campus key would let a participant collect XP from each of them without moving. Keyed on the booth, both event formats are covered by one rule."}, {"id": "readme_booth_type_duality", "label": "Two Booth Types in One Table (KAMPUS / JURUSAN)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "booth_type is KAMPUS (Event 2, one booth per university) or JURUSAN (Event 3, one booth per major), with a CHECK constraint requiring exactly one of university_id / major_id. Alumni are placed into the right booth automatically from the active event so they never choose."}, {"id": "readme_booth_checkin_grants_no_xp", "label": "Booth Poster Check-In Grants No XP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Participants scan a printed poster only to unlock DI_BOOTH material. If it awarded points, photographing the poster would earn XP for someone who never attended; XP comes only from an alumnus scanning the participant."}, {"id": "readme_session_status_switch", "label": "Sessions Gated by Status Switch, Not Clock Time", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A twenty-minute delay is normal at a school event; a time-based gate would close the scanners mid-queue. DRAFT/ACTIVE/CLOSED is the only thing that opens a scanner."}, {"id": "readme_xp_ledger_append_only", "label": "Append-Only XP Ledger", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A reversal is a new negative row. Level is computed from the ledger and never stored, so cancelling a visit corrects the level automatically. XP ceilings are re-checked server-side because a limit enforced only on the phone is not a limit."}, {"id": "readme_payment_outside_platform", "label": "Payment Handled Entirely Outside the Platform", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Administration collects cash or transfers and keeps their own book. No amount is stored anywhere, only who marked a registration settled and when, because a second set of figures here would eventually disagree with theirs."}, {"id": "readme_gated_payment_redirect", "label": "Gated Payment Redirect (GET /payments/buka)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "link_pembayaran and prefill_entry_id are never serialized into a participant-facing response. The form is reachable only through a server-side 302 issued after the profile is verified complete, with the registration code pre-filled, which makes forwarding the link self-defeating since a friend's payment would land under the sharer's code."}, {"id": "readme_offline_sync_idempotency", "label": "Offline Sync Answers 200 to Duplicates", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A phone that already delivered a scan and lost the response will retry; an error status makes it retry forever while a success ends the loop. Genuine rejections are recorded in sync_conflicts for committee review. Offline scanner payloads ship token_hash, never a raw QR token, so a stolen staff phone carries nothing that can mint a working badge."}, {"id": "readme_minor_participant_privacy", "label": "Minor-Participant Privacy Rules", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Participants are minors. Alumni see only participants who ticked the consent box and never a phone number; liaison officers see aggregate counts only. quiz_options.bobot (the answer key) is never sent to a client."}, {"id": "readme_audit_log_catat_audit", "label": "Audit Logging via catat_audit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every privileged mutation writes to audit_logs. Reversing a payment is Super Admin only, requires a written reason, and revokes the QR identity."}, {"id": "readme_soft_deactivate_form_fields", "label": "Form Fields Deactivated, Never Deleted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deleting a form field orphans the answers already submitted under it."}, {"id": "readme_configuration_in_database", "label": "Nothing a Division Might Change Lives in Code", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ticket wording, XP values, schedules, FAQ text, announcements, sponsors and form questions all live in the database so they can be changed from the admin dashboard without a deployment."}, {"id": "readme_mode_hemat", "label": "Economy Mode (mode_hemat)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Slows leaderboard and announcement polling and hides alumni statistics, but scanning, attendance and XP are never disabled."}, {"id": "readme_leaderboard_freeze", "label": "Leaderboard Freeze", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Locks the ranking before the ceremony so the winners cannot change mid-announcement. Ranking also carries tie-breakers, winner confirmation and an anomaly check (0009_leaderboard.sql)."}, {"id": "readme_health_check_touches_database", "label": "Health Check Deliberately Touches the Database", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A health check that only proves the Worker is running would report green while every check-in fails."}, {"id": "readme_registration_code_alphabet", "label": "Registration Code Alphabet Excludes 0 O 1 I L", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The code is read aloud across a desk and typed on a phone, and those are the characters that go wrong."}, {"id": "readme_migration_transaction_per_file", "label": "One Transaction per Migration File", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "39 tables across eleven files applied in filename order and recorded in _migrations; each file runs in its own transaction so a failure leaves the database at the last complete migration rather than half-applied."}, {"id": "readme_direct_port_migration_requirement", "label": "Migrations Require Direct Port 5432", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DATABASE_URL must use the direct port 5432 and never the pooler port 6543; the migration runner refuses it."}, {"id": "readme_demo_data_not_a_migration", "label": "Demo Data (db:contoh) Deliberately Not a Migration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fills events, sessions, universities, majors, university_majors, booths and sponsors with plausible rows so the frontend has something to render before the event division supplies real data. It is not a migration on purpose: demo rows must not reappear every time the database is rebuilt."}, {"id": "readme_module_why_comments", "label": "Per-Module Why Comments as Design Record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every module file opens with a comment explaining why it works the way it does, not what the code says; those comments are the design record and must be kept current when behaviour changes."}, {"id": "readme_schema_pinning_tests", "label": "Schema-Pinning Test Suite (tests/skema.test.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads the migration SQL and asserts the domain decisions are still in it, because they are the decisions easiest to undo by accident. Both suites run without a database."}, {"id": "readme_load_test_offline_flush_scenario", "label": "Load Test Scenario 7: Simultaneous Offline Queue Flush", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nine scenarios at 200 concurrent users, to be run no later than two weeks before the event; the scenario most worth attention is every phone flushing its offline queue at once when venue signal returns."}, {"id": "readme_no_automatic_backups", "label": "No Automatic Backups on Supabase Free Tier", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A daily dump is required because restoring from a backup that was never taken is not a recovery plan."}, {"id": "readme_infrastructure_document", "label": "Infrastructure Document", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_api_contract", "label": "API Contract (frontend-facing)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_frontend_pwa_boundary", "label": "Frontend PWA on Cloudflare Pages (separate ownership)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frontend, quiz engine, achievements, missions and the leaderboard UI are owned by other Web subdivision members. The leaderboard reads the XP ledger and never writes to it; that boundary is what keeps two people out of the same table. Same-origin deployment also means no CORS in production."}, {"id": "readme_same_origin_no_cors", "label": "Same-Origin Deployment Removes CORS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Lenovo\\CGTK-Digital-Experience-Platform\\